[38;2;124;124;124m$$\sum_{m=1}^n 5^{\omega(m)} \le \sum_{k=1}^n \lfloor n/k \rfloor \tau(k)^2 \le [0m[38;2;124;124;124m\sum_{m=1}^n 5^{\Omega(m)}$$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mwhere $\omega(m)$ is the number of distinct prime factors, $\Omega(m)$ is the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mtotal number of prime factors (with multiplicity), and $\tau(k)$ is the number [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mof divisors.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about the middle sum. We have:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$\sum_{k=1}^n \lfloor n/k \rfloor \tau(k)^2$$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNote that $\lfloor n/k \rfloor = \sum_{d=1}^n \mathbf{1}[k \mid d] \cdot [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\mathbf{1}[d \le n] / ...$. Actually, $\lfloor n/k \rfloor$ counts the number of[0m[38;2;124;124;124mmultiples of $k$ up to $n$. So $\lfloor n/k \rfloor = \sum_{m=1}^n \mathbf{1}[k [0m[38;2;124;124;124m\mid m]$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$\sum_{k=1}^n \lfloor n/k \rfloor \tau(k)^2 = \sum_{k=1}^n \sum_{m=1}^n [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\mathbf{1}[k \mid m] \tau(k)^2 = \sum_{m=1}^n \sum_{k \mid m, k \le n} [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\tau(k)^2$$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSince $k \mid m$ and $m \le n$ implies $k \le m \le n$, we have:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$= \sum_{m=1}^n \sum_{k \mid m} \tau(k)^2$$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo the middle sum equals $\sum_{m=1}^n f(m)$ where $f(m) = \sum_{k \mid m} [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\tau(k)^2$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow I need to show that $5^{\omega(m)} \le f(m) \le 5^{\Omega(m)}$ for all $m$.[0m

