[38;2;124;124;124m- $\Omega(p^a) = a$, so $5^{\Omega(p^a)} = 5^a$.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- The divisors of $p^a$ are $1, p, p^2, \ldots, p^a$, with $\tau(p^j) = j+1$.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- So $f(p^a) = \sum_{j=0}^a \tau(p^j)^2 = \sum_{j=0}^a (j+1)^2 = \sum_{i=1}[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m^{a+1} i^2 = \frac{(a+1)(a+2)(2a+3)}{6}$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWe need to show:[0m
